# Pruebas con la extensión "REST Client" de VS Code (o el cliente HTTP de Rider/VS).
@base = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Registro -> 201 { id, email }
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "gloria@correo.com", "password": "secreto123" }

### 2. Registro repetido -> 409
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "gloria@correo.com", "password": "secreto123" }

### 3. Login -> 200 { access_token }
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "gloria@correo.com", "password": "secreto123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 4. Login con clave incorrecta -> 401
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "gloria@correo.com", "password": "mala" }

### 5. Listado (público) -> 200 { data, total, page, limit, items, totalPages }
GET {{base}}/juegos

### 6. Búsqueda por nombre + paginación
GET {{base}}/juegos?search=hollow&page=1&limit=5

### 7. Detalle -> 200 / 404
GET {{base}}/juegos/1

### 8. Crear SIN token -> 401
POST {{base}}/juegos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "Zelda", "imagen": "https://ejemplo.com/zelda.jpg", "categoria": "Aventura" }

### 9. Crear CON token -> 201
POST {{base}}/juegos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "Zelda", "imagen": "https://ejemplo.com/zelda.jpg", "categoria": "Aventura" }

### 10. Crear inválido (falta nombre) -> 400 { message: [...], error, statusCode }
POST {{base}}/juegos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "imagen": "x", "categoria": "Aventura" }

### 11. Editar parcialmente -> 200
PATCH {{base}}/juegos/14
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "Zelda: Ocarina of Time" }

### 12. Eliminar -> 204
DELETE {{base}}/juegos/14
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Eliminar inexistente -> 404
DELETE {{base}}/juegos/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
